  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF PRIORITY TORTOISE AND FRESHWATER TURTLE SPECIES IN VIETNAM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO HELP CONSERVE SEVEN OF THE WORLD S MOST CRITICALLY ENDANGERED SPECIES, ONE OF WHICH IS SWINHOE S SOFTSHELL TURTLE. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) SECURING A BREEDING GROUP FOR THE SWINHOE S SOFTSHELL TURTLE WITH ONLY THREE KNOWN LIVING ANIMALS, TWO IN THE WILD AND ONE IN A ZOO IN CHINA (2) PROMOTING CONSERVATION OF THE INDOCHINESE BOX TURTLE IN PUMAT NATIONAL PARK (3) BOLSTERING A POPULATION OF BOURRET S BOX TURTLE THROUGH REINTRODUCTION (4) INITIATING STEPS TO CREATE AN EXPANDED PROTECTED AREA FOR THE SOUTHERN VIETNAMESE BOX TURTLE (5) WORKING TO REESTABLISH A WILD POPULATION OF THE ENDEMIC VIETNAMESE POND TURTLE (6) DETERMINING THE DISTRIBUTION OF ZHOU S BOX TURTLE IN NORTHERN VIETNAM, WHICH IS ONLY KNOWN FROM ONE CAPTIVE SPECIMEN (7) IDENTIFYING NESTING SITES FOR THE ASIAN GIANT SOFTSHELL TURTLE IN SEKONG RIVER BASIN, LAO PDR.</narrative>
  </description>
